"type":"word","value":"-c"},{"type":"string","value":"\"\nimport sys,json\nd=json.load(sys.stdin)\ndesign=d['design']\nidx=design.find('## Data Model')\nprint(design[idx:idx+4500])\n\""}],"fullText":"python3 -c \"\nimport sys,json\nd=json.load(sys.stdin)\ndesign=d['design']\nidx=design.find('## Data Model')\nprint(design[idx:idx+4500])\n\""}],"hasRedirects":true,"hasCommandSubstitution":false,"allRedirectsAreDevNull":true,"redirects":[{"operator":">&","destinationFds":[2],"targetNodeType":"number","targetText":"1"}]},"fileOutputThresholdBytes":"40000","isBackground":false,"skipApproval":false,"timeoutBehavior":"TIMEOUT_BEHAVIOR_BACKGROUND","hardTimeout":86400000,"description":"Check /app path and design data model","closeStdin":true,"conversationId":"6b0bb5d8-2e5d-4c96-912d-ac99e088e5d4","adminCommandDenylist":[]},"result":{"success":{"command":"ls -la /app 2>&1; head -c 200 /work/ws/worktrees/app/backend-dev-1/start.sh; echo; grep -n HUDDLE\\|data\\|DB /work/ws/worktrees/app/backend-dev-1/start.sh; readlink -f /work/ws/worktrees/app/backend-dev-1; loom data show MARATHON-3 --output json | python3 -c \"\nimport sys,json\nd=json.load(sys.stdin)\ndesign=d['design']\nidx=design.find('## Data Model')\nprint(design[idx:idx+4500])\n\"","workingDirectory":"","exitCode":0,"signal":"","stdout":"total 20\ndrwxr-xr-x. 1 root root  110 Aug 22 19:39 .\ndr-xr-xr-x. 1 root root  131 Aug 22 19:27 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x. 9 root root 4096 Aug 22 19:39 .git\ndrwxr-xr-x. 1 root root   65 Aug 22 19:40 data\n-rw-r--r--. 1 root root  132 Aug 22 19:39 package.json\n-rw-r--r--. 1 root root  116 Aug 22 19:39 redis.conf\ndrwxr-xr-x. 2 root root   39 Aug 22 19:39 server\n-rwxr-xr-x. 1 root root 2596 Aug 22 19:39 start.sh\ndrwxr-xr-x. 2 root root   82 Aug 22 19:39 test\n-rwxr-xr-x. 1 root root  558 Aug  1 00:43 timer.sh\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Huddle cluster supervisor: Redis + three HTTP nodes. Stays in the foreground.\nset -u\n\nAPP_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd)\"\ncd \"$APP_DIR\" || exit 1\n\nNODE_BIN=\"${NODE_BIN:-}\"\ni\n/work/ws/worktrees/app/backend-dev-1\n## Data Model\n\n### Schema change\n**New** SQLite DB `/app/data/huddle.db` (greenfield; backward compatible with empty `/app/data/`).\n\n#### Table `users`\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\n|--------|------|------|-------|\n| `id` | TEXT | NOT NULL PK | UUID |\n| `username` | TEXT | NOT NULL | Original casing |\n| `username_lower` | TEXT | NOT NULL UNIQUE | `lower(username)` for conflict/login |\n| `password_salt` | TEXT | NOT NULL | hex or base64 |\n| `password_hash` | TEXT | NOT NULL | scrypt output encoding |\n| `display_name` | TEXT | NOT NULL | |\n| `timezone` | TEXT | NOT NULL DEFAULT `'UTC'` | |\n| `avatar_url` | TEXT | NOT NULL DEFAULT `''` | |\n| `status_text` | TEXT | NOT NULL DEFAULT `''` | |\n| `status_emoji` | TEXT | NOT NULL DEFAULT `''` | |\n| `created_at` | TEXT | NOT NULL | RFC3339 UTC |\n\n#### Table `tokens`\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\n|--------|------|------|-------|\n| `token` | TEXT | NOT NULL PK | Opaque bearer (≥16 chars) |\n| `user_id` | TEXT | NOT NULL | FK → `users.id` |\n| `created_at` | TEXT | NOT NULL | RFC3339 UTC |\n\nIndexes: PK/UNIQUE as above; optional index `tokens(user_id)` for future logout-all (not required this task).\n\n**Migrations:** On worker boot, `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS` + WAL pragmas. No versioned migration framework required yet; keep DDL in one module (`server/db.js`) so MARATHON-4+ can extend columns carefully.\n\n**Password material and salts never appear in HTTP responses.**\n\n## Files to Create / Files to Modify\n\n### Create\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/db.js` | Open `/app/data/huddle.db`, ensure `/app/data` exists, set `journal_mode=WAL`, `busy_timeout`, run DDL for `users`/`tokens`, export `getDb()` |\n| `server/auth/passwords.js` | `hashPassword(password) → {salt, hash}`, `verifyPassword(password, salt, hash) → boolean` using `crypto.scrypt` (sync or promisified consistently) |\n| `server/auth/tokens.js` | `issueToken(userId) → string` (insert row); `findUserIdByToken(token) → string \\| null` |\n| `server/auth/users.js` | `createUser(...)`, `findUserByUsername(username)`, `publicUser(row) → UserObj` |\n| `server/auth/middleware.js` | `resolveBearerUser`, `requireUser` |\n| `server/auth/routes.js` | Handlers for register, login, me; JSON parse helper; status codes per contract |\n| `server/httpUtil.js` (optional) | `readJson(req)`, `sendJson(res, status, body)` shared with health — only if not already present from MARATHON-2 |\n\n### Modify\n| File | Change |\n|------|--------|\n| `server/index.js` | Route `POST /api/auth/register`, `POST /api/auth/login`, `GET /api/auth/me` before generic 404; keep `GET /api/health` behavior unchanged; initialize DB once at process start (fail boot if DB cannot open) |\n| `package.json` | No new dependencies required; may note Node ≥22 for `node:sqlite` |\n| `start.sh` | **No change required** if it already creates `/app/data` (MARATHON-2). If not yet implemented when this lands, ensure `mkdir -p /app/data` remains. Do not move Redis dir. |\n\n### Do not modify\n| File | Reason |\n|------|--------|\n| `timer.sh` | Harness timer |\n| SPA / static HTML | MARATHON-21 |\n\n## Sequencing and Cross-Task Seams\n\n### Within this task\n1. `db.js` + DDL  \n2. passwords / users / tokens  \n3. middleware  \n4. routes + wire `index.js`  \n5. Cross-node manual check (register :8000 → me :8001)\n\n### Parallelism\n- Backend implementer owns all files above.\n- Frontend MARATHON-21 **architecture** can proceed from contracts C1–C3; **implementation** of SPA auth UI should land after (or against mocked) these endpoints.\n- MARATHON-4 (profiles) extends `users` columns usage and adds routes; must reuse `UserObj` + `requireUser`.\n- MARATHON-5+ all depend on bearer middleware + durable users.\n\n### Seams this task owns\n| Seam | Downstream |\n|------|------------|\n| C1/C2/C3 HTTP auth | MARATHON-21 SPA; QA grader |\n| `UserObj` shape | MARATHON-4, channel members, messages `author`, WS `user.updated` |\n| Session table / `resolveBearerUser` | MARATHON-5…20 authenticated APIs; WS `?token=`; IRC `PASS` |\n| `/app/data/huddle.db` | All durable domain tables (siblings add tables, do not fork a second user DB) |\n\n### Build order vs siblings\n- **Blocked on:** MARATHON-2 bootstrap (ports, `server/index.js`, `/app/data`). If MARATHON-2 is not merged, implementer still codes against its file layout and integrates when bootstrap lands.\n- **Blocks:** MARATHON-5, MARATHON-11, MARATHON-21 (declared dependents), and practically every authenticated task.\n\n### Split follow-ups (do not do here)\n| Cut | Ow\n","stderr":"time=2026-08-22T19:46:10.942Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:38569\n","executionTime":129,"interleavedOutput":"total 20\ndrwxr-xr-x. 1 root root  110 Aug 22 19:39 .\ndr-xr-xr-x. 1 root root  131 Aug 22 19:27 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x. 9 root root 4096 Aug 22 19:39 .git\ndrwxr-xr-x. 1 root root   65 Aug 22 19:40 data\n-rw-r--r--. 1 root root  132 Aug 22 19:39 package.json\n-rw-r--r--. 1 root root  116 Aug 22 19:39 redis.conf\ndrwxr-xr-x. 2 root root   39 Aug 22 19:39 server\n-rwxr-xr-x. 1 root root 2596 Aug 22 19:39 start.sh\ndrwxr-xr-x. 2 root root   82 Aug 22 19:39 test\n-rwxr-xr-x. 1 root root  558 Aug  1 00:43 timer.sh\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Huddle cluster supervisor: Redis + three HTTP nodes. Stays in the foreground.\nset -u\n\nAPP_DIR=\"$(cd \"$(dirname \"$0\")\" && pwd)\"\ncd \"$APP_DIR\" || exit 1\n\nNODE_BIN=\"${NODE_BIN:-}\"\ni\n/work/ws/worktrees/app/backend-dev-1\ntime=2026-08-22T19:46:10.942Z level=INFO msg=\"opened existing embedded fleet-db client\" url=http://127.0.0.1:38569\n## Data Model\n\n### Schema change\n**New** SQLite DB `/app/data/huddle.db` (greenfield; backward compatible with empty `/app/data/`).\n\n#### Table `users`\n| Column | Type | Null | Notes |\n|--------|------|------|-------|\n| `id` | TEXT | NOT NULL PK | UUID |\n| `username` |